            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Matt: can you look at this build failure and let me know what you'd like done?  There are a bunch of 'auto' features, some of which conflict with each other.  I'm not sure what you'd like as the default set for CI."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I think we want phal=enabled and also openfsi=enabled, that's what we'll use for everything going forward"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "```\n/var/jenkins-openbmc/workspace/ci-repository/openbmc/openpower-proc-control > meson setup --reconfigure build -Db_colorout=never -Dwerror=true -Dwarning_level=3 -Ddebug=true -Doptimization=g \n\n\nmeson.build:69:4: ERROR: Problem encountered: phal and p9 cannot be selected at the same time\n```\n\nLooks like both features (phal and p9) are enabled/auto, which is not allowed\n\nThe \"auto_feature\" default value is \"auto\" so I guess the \"auto\" value is set and we are getting true from \"allowed()\" for both features?"
                }
            ],
